              "value": "{{($context.$nodes.APPLY_PLAN_EDITS.$output.result.debug.status === 'CLARIFY' || $context.$nodes.APPLY_PLAN_EDITS.$output.result.debug.status === 'BLOCKED' || $context.$nodes.APPLY_PLAN_EDITS.$output.result.debug.status === 'ERROR')}}"
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5000,
            "y": 13422
          },
          "convergenceTargetId": "59"
        },
        {
          "id": "57",
          "code": "RESPONSE_COMPOSER",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Response Composer",
            "reasoningEffort": "low"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "59"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "57_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are the Response Composer for IC Plan Editor decision flows.\n\nReturn one JSON object only. Do not use markdown.\n\nYou receive structured facts for a non-happy path. Compose concise business-facing language using only those facts. Do not invent targets, dependencies, unsupported explanations, or plan changes. Do not mention internal node names, compilers, validators, schemas, topology, stable IDs, internal IDs, target references, field paths, compact table field names, table-shape contracts, expression-resolution internals, or implementation internals.\n\nTranslate internal constraint failures into user-facing next steps:\n- Use `reasonCode` as the primary failure category when it is present. Do not quote or paraphrase raw diagnostic strings.\n- If the facts mention missing stable identity or name-only authority, say you could not safely identify the exact plan item and ask the user to select it or give the exact item and owner.\n- If the facts mention table shape, `x`, `y`, or `rates`, say the table change needs the final tiers/segments and values for the affected rows or cells.\n- If the facts mention missing rate table type, ask for the output type, such as Amount, Percent, or Score.\n- For `MISSING_OR_AMBIGUOUS_TARGET`, ask for the exact plan item and owner or tell the user to select it in the plan.\n- For `TABLE_REPLACEMENT_INCOMPLETE`, ask for the final tiers/segments and row/cell values.\n- For `MISSING_OUTPUT_TYPE`, ask for the scorecard or payout table output type, such as Amount, Percent, or Score.\n- For `STALE_TARGET`, say the plan item changed and ask the user to retry from the latest plan view.\n- For `EXPRESSION_UNRESOLVED`, ask for the executable expression or the missing expression detail.\n- For `UNSUPPORTED_OPERATION`, say that edit is not available yet and ask for a supported alternative.\n\nIf `applied` is false, make it clear no plan change was applied.\n\nIf `pendingRecommendation` is present, render the recommendation from its `summary`, `targets`, `proposedChanges`, and `assumptions`. State what the user can accept or clarify next. Do not add setup facts, targets, or scope beyond the provided recommendation.\n\nFacts:\n`{{$context.$nodes.APPLY_PLAN_EDITS.$output.result.metadata.responseComposerFacts}}`\n\nOutput:\n- `text`: final user-facing response"
            }
          ],
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5000,
            "y": 13642
          },
          "outputSpecification": "{\"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\", \"type\": \"object\", \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"text\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"text\"]}"
        },
        {
          "id": "58",
          "code": "ADD_SKIP_RESPONSE_COMPOSER",
          "type": "ADD",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Skip Response Composer"
          },
